=== MDV-P8-008
title: Dental practitioner licences: dental councils in India and dental licences in the UAE, printed on prescriptions
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Owner, Dentist
labels: dental, licence, identity
estimate: 2
weeks: 52
depends: MDV-P8-001, MDV-P1-065
confidence: 80 | Extends the owner attestation from P1-065; the authority lists are known.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
The owner attests a dentist the same way as a doctor (P1-065), but the authority list offers the Dental Council of India and the state dental councils (India) and the dental licence of DHA, DOH or MOHAP (UAE). The role Dentist gets the doctor's clinical capabilities.
ac:
- A dentist can be added with a dental council registration number, authority and expiry; the medical-only authorities are not required.
- The prescription and signed note print the dental registration number and authority.
- Licence expiry reminders (P1-010) cover dental licences.
- Server-side authorisation tests prove a Dentist has the same clinical access as a Doctor and no more.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Pick up from DentalERP: nothing; it has no licence fields. Build on P1-065.

=== MDV-P8-009
title: Book by chair and procedure length: chairs as bookable resources, durations per dental procedure
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Dentist, Dental assistant, Receptionist
labels: dental, scheduling, booking
estimate: 4
weeks: 52-53
depends: MDV-P8-008, MDV-P1-011, MDV-P1-022
confidence: 70 | Rooms and resources exist in schedule templates; booking still follows the doctor.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
Each dental chair is a resource with its own hours. A dental procedure carries a default duration (for example root canal 60 min, scaling 30 min) that sets the appointment length. An appointment holds a dentist and a chair.
ac:
- A booking reserves both the dentist and the chair; neither can be double-booked (same guard as P1-022, tested under concurrency).
- Choosing a procedure sets the slot length; reception can lengthen it.
- The day view can be shown by chair as well as by dentist, in English and Arabic.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Pick up from DentalERP: `chairNumber` on Appointment and `defaultDuration` on Procedure (prisma/schema.prisma) show the idea only; chairs there are a number, not a resource with hours.
- Data to take: the duration of each procedure from prisma/seed-data/IN/procedures.ts (feeds P8-010).

=== MDV-P8-010
status: Done
progress:
- Merged [PR #1437](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/1437): 76 India dental procedures (adapted from DentalERP, MIT) with code, length, editable INR price, SAC 999312 and GST on the 8 cosmetic rows; loaded from Settings › Dental in one transaction with one audit event; loading again adds nothing; India only
- Needs a person: a dentist signs off the 76 fees and a chartered accountant confirms the GST treatment (MDV-P4-031); see the session handoff
title: Dental services and fees list
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Owner
labels: dental, billing, catalogue
estimate: 2
weeks: 53
depends: MDV-P8-008, MDV-P4-002
confidence: 65 | Depends on the P4 services catalogue; UAE claim codes need a licence check.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
A starter list of dental procedures (consultation, scaling, filling by surfaces, root canal by canals, extraction, crown, bridge, denture, implant stages, orthodontic visits) loaded into the services catalogue with editable fees. India consultations stay GST-exempt; UAE carries VAT and the code set the payer requires.
ac:
- The owner can load, edit and price the dental list from Settings → Services.
- Fees are integer minor units with currency (AGENTS.md 3.4).
- The licence terms of any UAE dental code set are recorded before it is loaded.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Data to take: prisma/seed-data/IN/procedures.ts, 76 dental procedures with code, name, category, duration, INR price, pre and post instructions. Convert prices to integer paise; map the 10 `ProcedureCategory` values (Diagnostic, Preventive, Restorative, Endodontic, Periodontic, Prosthodontic, Orthodontic, Oral surgery, Cosmetic, Emergency) to service groups. A dentist reviews names and default fees before release.
- No UAE set exists there (only IN, US, DE); the UAE list and payer codes are new work.
- Code to read: app/api/procedures, app/api/settings/procedures (catalogue screens); lib/treatment-utils.ts `procedureCategoryConfig` for labels.

=== MDV-P8-011
status: Done
progress:
- Merged [PR #1437](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/1437): FDI tooth chart (permanent, primary, mixed) drawn as real teeth with the five surfaces of the design (DN-02), codes always printed, history per tooth; findings append-only (the database refuses UPDATE), recorded in an open consultation; the same chart on the dental PDF; ToothChart in @medvya/ui; behind `clinical.dental` (Internal release stage)
- Needs a person: a dentist signs off the condition list and surfaces (`DentalRules.SignOff`) and the open questions on the design canvas before the feature leaves the Internal stage
title: Tooth chart: FDI numbering, adult and milk teeth, surfaces and conditions, with history per tooth
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Dentist
labels: dental, chart, clinical
estimate: 6
weeks: 53-55
depends: MDV-P8-008, MDV-P2-004
confidence: 60 | New clinical component; needs a dentist to approve the condition list.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
A tooth chart on the patient record and the consultation: FDI two-digit numbering, permanent, primary and mixed dentition, five surfaces per tooth, and conditions (caries, filling, crown, root canal treated, missing, implant, bridge, mobile, fractured). Each change is recorded with who, when and the visit, as part of the signed note.
ac:
- A dentist can mark a condition on a tooth and surface with a mouse, a touch screen or the keyboard alone.
- A condition is shown by a symbol and words, never by colour alone (AGENTS.md 1.5).
- Signed findings are not edited; a correction is an addendum.
- Each new domain property carries a data classification; tenant isolation tests cover the new tables.
- Checked in a browser in English and Arabic (right to left keeps FDI numbers in their quadrants), axe clean.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Code to port (layout only): components/dental-chart/dental-chart.tsx (611 lines) and components/treatments/dental-chart.tsx (523 lines, a second variant); FDI quadrant arrays, tooth names and surface labels in lib/treatment-utils.ts (`toothNumbers`, `toothNames`, `toothSurfaceLabels`, `toothConditionConfig`).
- Data to take: the `ToothCondition` list (14 values) and the 5-surface model of `DentalChartEntry` in prisma/schema.prisma; API shape in app/api/dental-chart.
- Do not take: conditions shown by colour only (bg-red-500 etc.) break AGENTS.md 1.5; adult teeth only (no 51 to 85); entries are edited in place, while Medvya needs signed, append-only findings. Rebuild on @medvya/ui.

=== MDV-P8-012
status: Done
progress:
- Merged [PR #1437](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/1437): plan items from the services list per tooth or whole mouth in phases 1–9; Planned → In progress → Done or Declined with a reason, never deleted; estimate without declined items; acceptance with who, how and when, and "changed since accepted"; a done item is one suggested line on the visit's bill, never billed twice
- Follow-up: a waive reason for a removed suggested line, and an "unbilled done items" list for items done after the bill is issued
title: Dental treatment plan: items per tooth, phases, cost estimate and patient acceptance
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Dentist, Patient, Receptionist
labels: dental, treatment-plan, billing
estimate: 5
weeks: 55-56
depends: MDV-P8-010, MDV-P8-011, MDV-P4-004
confidence: 60 | Links clinical plan to charge capture; estimate wording needs a dentist.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
From the tooth chart the dentist builds a plan: procedure items on teeth and surfaces, grouped in phases, priced from the dental list. The patient sees and accepts the estimate (printed or on a tablet). Items move Planned → In progress → Done, and a done item becomes a charge on the visit invoice.
ac:
- The estimate shows each item, its tooth and its fee, and a total; acceptance records who accepted and when.
- A done item creates exactly one charge (idempotent), with the fee version of the day.
- Declined or postponed items stay on the plan with a reason.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Code to read: components/treatments/treatment-plan-editor.tsx (656 lines), app/api/treatment-plans; models `TreatmentPlan` and `TreatmentPlanItem` (tooth numbers, priority, estimated cost, status) in prisma/schema.prisma; status labels in lib/treatment-utils.ts.
- Missing there and new here: phases, patient acceptance with who and when, idempotent charge on done. `toothNumbers` is a free string there; use a typed list of FDI codes and surfaces.

