=== MDV-P8-014
title: Medical history check before dental treatment
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: MUST
roles: Dentist, Dental assistant, Receptionist
labels: dental, safety, clinical
estimate: 2
weeks: 53
depends: MDV-P8-008, MDV-P2-004, MDV-P2-008
confidence: 75 | Reuses chart history and allergies; the question list needs a dentist.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
At each treatment visit the assistant or dentist confirms the history that matters for dental care: anticoagulants or antiplatelets, diabetes, pregnancy, heart conditions and endocarditis risk, bisphosphonates, and local anaesthetic allergy. Nurse vitals stay optional for a dental clinic.
ac:
- A treatment visit shows the history check with the date it was last confirmed.
- An answer that raises risk shows a warning in words on the consultation before the plan item can be started.
- The check is recorded on the visit and audited.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Pick up from DentalERP: `MedicalHistory` model fields as a checklist starting point; the dental risk questions are new and need a dentist.

=== MDV-P8-015
title: Dental note template and dental medicines in the formulary
type: Task
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: SHOULD
roles: Dentist, Dental assistant, Receptionist
labels: dental, templates, formulary
estimate: 2
weeks: 53
depends: MDV-P2-025, MDV-P2-014
confidence: 75 | Uses the existing template engine and admin-added medicines.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
A dental template in the P2-025 engine (chief complaint, extra-oral and intra-oral examination, findings from the tooth chart, plan, advice) and dental items in the formulary (local anaesthetics such as lignocaine with adrenaline, chlorhexidine mouthwash, common dental analgesics and antibiotics).
ac:
- The owner can pick the dental template as the clinic default.
- Dental medicines are searchable and carry their regulatory class.
- A dentist approves the template and the medicine list.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Data to take: prisma/seed-data/IN/medications.ts, 8 dental medicines (amoxicillin, ibuprofen, paracetamol, metronidazole, chlorhexidine mouthwash, diclofenac, omeprazole, clindamycin) with default dose, frequency and duration. No local anaesthetic in any seed set: lignocaine with adrenaline is new. Each item still needs its Schedule class (ADR-015).
- Template fields to read: components/treatments/treatment-editor.tsx (chief complaint, findings, diagnosis, procedure notes, materials used).

=== MDV-P8-016
title: Dental imaging: X-rays and photos on the tooth, with a viewer
type: Story
epic: MDV-P8-E02
prd: P8-06
priority: SHOULD
roles: Dentist, Dental assistant, Receptionist
labels: dental, imaging, documents
estimate: 4
weeks: 57-58
depends: MDV-P8-011, MDV-P2-006
confidence: 50 | Upload and viewer build on documents; CBCT (DICOM) needs a spike.
sources: Dentist review of the clinic journey (whiteboard, 15 Nov 2026)
desc:
Intraoral X-rays (IOPA/RVG), OPG and intraoral photos uploaded through the documents pipeline (malware scan, time-limited viewer) and attached to one or more teeth and the visit; viewer with zoom, brightness and contrast; before/after comparison. CBCT and DICOM sensor import start as a spike.
ac:
- An image can be attached to teeth and opened from the tooth chart.
- Images never appear in URLs with patient data; links are time-limited (P2-006 rules).
- A spike records the CBCT/DICOM option and its cost.
notes:
- Source: DentalERP (github.com/abinauv/dental-erp, MIT; reference reviewed 17 Nov 2026).
- Code to port: components/imaging/image-viewer.tsx (zoom, brightness, contrast), image-compare.tsx (before/after), image-annotator.tsx. Leave dental-3d-viewer.tsx for the CBCT spike.
- Its uploads go to local disk (app/api/uploads); use the Medvya documents pipeline (P2-006) instead.

